UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_54116078717348
DTSTART:20261017T160000Z
DTEND:20261017T180000Z
DESCRIPTION:Inspired by Honoré Daumier’s work in “Friendly Arbitration\,” we will explore D.I.Y. Kitchen Lithography! Using aluminum foil and soda\, we will make illustrations directly on foil and print multiple copies of your designs. Lithography is based on the principle that water and oil do not mix\; we will use wax-based pigments to draw our illustrations\, then use water as a resist to apply ink.  \n\nPre-registration is required\; the link is in our linkin.bio. Parking will be available in the Call St Garage\, and all materials will be provided. “Friendly Arbitration” is on view at MoFA until Saturday\, December 12\, 2026. We will host many printmaking workshops while the exhibition is on display\, so keep an eye out!
GEO:30.444141;-84.29018
LOCATION:Museum of Fine Arts \, Conference Room/Courtyard 
SUMMARY:Make it with MoFA: D.I.Y. Kitchen Lithography
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/make-it-with-mofa-diy-kitchen-lithography-2384
CATEGORIES:Arts/Entertainment
CATEGORIES:Free to the Public
CATEGORIES:Academic/Registrar
