DESCRIPTION:The Department of Modern Languages and Linguistics and the Department of Art History invite you to a book talk with Professor Tenley Bick\nMichelangelo Pistoletto: Figuration and Cultural Politics\nYALE UNIVERSITY PRESS\, 2025\n\n\nAfter an overview of her book\, Dr. Bick turns to Pistoletto's understudied experiments in real and representational living in his collaborative performance works of the late 1960s and 1970s\, and to "direct\, lived action" as an antiauthoritarian\, world-staging practice.\nAll are welcome.\n\nWHEN: Monday\, October 19 at 5 PM\nWHERE: Diffenbaugh 009\nMORE INFO: email [contact removed]
GEO:30.440072;-84.291219
LOCATION:Diffenbaugh Building (DIF)\, 009
SUMMARY:Book Talk with Tenley Bick
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.fsu.edu/event/book-talk-with-tenley-bick
CATEGORIES:Special Events
CATEGORIES:Speakers & Lectures
END:VEVENT
